In-Reply-To: <MNNTVGxPnos.hTQdntDMAQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <MNNTVGxPnos.hTQdntDMAQAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/MNNTVGxPnos/m/JspBmv-eBAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Minor differences in the DIC is to be expected, simply because of the
parallel computing. If the posterior is very flat, then the impact can
be larger.  if you expect a flat posterior, you can try to do

r = inla(...)
r = inla.rerun(r)

which will restart at the current mode, which usually would stabalize
the results.

If there are any differences beyond this, please let me know.

Best
H

